{"name":"Broiled Flounder","hex":"#ffdd88","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"broiled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of broil"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broiled"},{"term":"flounder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A European species of flatfish having dull brown colouring with reddish-brown blotches; fluke, European flounder (Platichthys flesus).","Any of various flatfish of the family Pleuronectidae or Bothidae."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act clumsily or confused; to struggle or be flustered.","To flop around as a fish out of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flounder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grilling","blocks":[{"text":"Grilling is a form of cooking that involves heat applied to the surface of food, commonly from above, below or from the side. Grilling usually involves a significant amount of direct, radiant heat, and tends to be used for cooking meat and vegetables quickly. Food to be grilled is cooked on a grill, using a cast iron/frying pan, or a grill pan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Grillen_-_BBQ_-_Barbeque_-_Fleisch_auf_dem_Grill.jpg/330px-Grillen_-_BBQ_-_Barbeque_-_Fleisch_auf_dem_Grill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grilling","wikidata":"Q264619"},{"title":"Flounder","blocks":[{"text":"Flounders are a group of flatfish species. They are demersal fish, found at the bottom of oceans around the world; some species will also enter estuaries."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Pseudopleuronectes_americanus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flounder","wikidata":"Q4246303"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Hamburguesas_grill.jpg/500px-Hamburguesas_gr